60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A is too risky; the distance will spike transport costs and the non-refundable headcount is a financial liability. Option B is safer for the budget, but Option C offers a low-cost, inclusive rate.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is out because of the cooking burden and fragmented training hours. Option C is a nightmare to book. Option A removes the labor burden from us, which is a huge relief for the organizers.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option A is the only one that guarantees we all sleep in the same place, which is essential for cohesion. Option B fails this completely, and Option C's crowded dorms might hinder the quality of our bonding.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option C's crowded rooms and strict rules would be detrimental to rest. Option B's fragmented schedule is equally problematic. Option A seems the most conducive to both recovery and a coherent training flow.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A is logically the most risky due to the non-refundable deposit and high transport costs. Option C is the most stable financially, though the booking process is tedious. Option B is inefficient for training.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, @Minako, @Jonathan, you all seem to favor Option A, but the financial risk is too high. If we have late cancellations, the remaining members pay. I cannot support a plan with such unpredictable costs.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Minako"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, I understand your caution, but we must consider the human cost. If we choose C, the organizers are crushed by paperwork. If we choose B, we are crushed by cooking. A is the only sustainable choice for us.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, the financial risk is a concern, but the risk of the club falling apart is greater. Option A ensures we stay together and removes the burden from the organizers. It is the only choice that addresses the social decay.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, while I share your desire for stability, the physical and mental exhaustion from Options B and C would undermine the entire purpose of the camp. Option A provides the peace and recovery we need to actually improve.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, I agree that the financial risk of Option A is illogical. However, Option B is impractical for training and Option C's booking process is a liability. We must decide if the social and physical benefits of A outweigh the financial risks.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the risk isn't just illogical; it's a liability I can't ignore. However, if everyone else is willing to accept the financial risk to avoid burnout and social decay, I may have to concede. But I still strongly prefer C.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, I appreciate your willingness to concede. The administrative burden of C is simply too high for us to bear again. Option A is the only one that protects the organizers' time and the members' sanity.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Ryuji, thank you for being flexible. We cannot let the club fracture over a budget gap. Option A is the only way to ensure the cohesion we need to survive as a group. I vote for A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Minako. The quality of our rest and the coherence of our training are non-negotiable for a successful camp. Option A is the only choice that preserves our well-being. I vote for A.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, while the financial risk of Option A is significant, the logical failures of B and C are more immediate. To ensure the camp's actual success and the organizers' sanity, A is the most viable. I vote for A.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I still have deep reservations about the financial instability of Option A, but I cannot ignore the consensus. To avoid burnout and social collapse, I will concede. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I am glad we reached a consensus. Prioritizing the organizers' well-being and the members' sanity is the only way to make this sustainable. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,I am glad we could prioritize the club's future and the health of our community. Ensuring we all stay together is the right decision. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I am pleased that we have found a path that prioritizes the well-being of all members. A peaceful environment is the foundation of growth. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"The decision is logically sound given the constraints. While the financial risk remains, it is the only option that doesn't compromise our training or the organizers' health. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
